---
import PhotoCarousel from './PhotoCarousel.astro';
import alps from '../assets/blog/travel-alps.jpg';
import wing from '../assets/blog/travel-wing.jpg';
import street from '../assets/blog/travel-street.jpg';
import coast from '../assets/blog/travel-coast.jpg';

const slides = [
  {
    src: alps.src,
    alt: 'A turquoise alpine lake with chalets along the shore and steep mountains behind it',
    caption: 'Morning on an alpine lake',
  },
  {
    src: wing.src,
    alt: 'An airplane wing above a layer of clouds lit by sunrise',
    caption: 'Sunrise from the window seat',
  },
  {
    src: street.src,
    alt: 'A narrow cobblestone street at dusk with warm shop lights reflecting on wet stones',
    caption: 'The street after the lamps come on',
  },
  {
    src: coast.src,
    alt: 'A cliff path above a deep blue sea, with a white village farther along the coast',
    caption: 'The path above the coast',
  },
];
---

<section class="travel-blog" id="travel" aria-labelledby="travel-heading">
  <div class="travel-blog-inner">
    <p class="kicker">Travel</p>
    <h2 id="travel-heading">A layover worth keeping</h2>
    <p class="dek">
      Sample post. Replace this copy and the photos when you have a trip of your own to write up.
    </p>
    <PhotoCarousel slides={slides} />
    <article>
      <p>
        The cheaper fare was the one with a stop. The schedule called it a connection. From the
        window it looked like a place worth standing in, so the connection became the trip: one
        night, a walk before breakfast, and a flight home after the light changed.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the small habit this section is here for. A photo, a place, and a few lines about
        why the stop was better than the nonstop. Scroll the pictures above, then write the next
        one in the same shape.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .travel-blog {
    background: #edeff2;
    color: #191721;
    padding: 72px 24px 88px;
  }

  .travel-blog-inner {
    max-width: 880px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-family: 'Sintony', sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #2364aa;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'Sintony', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .dek {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 14px 0 28px;
    font-family: 'Sintony', sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #3c4048;
  }

  article {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 4px solid #fec601;
  }

  article p {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    max-width: 40rem;
    font-family: 'Sintony', sans-serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
